      "side": 1,
      "message": "This completely breaks the point of the /dev/google directory structure.  :)  If you just want a number associated with each serial stream you can get that from the /dev/ttyUSB? that is also already generated.  The point of the GOOGLE_CCD_NAME is to give you a unique path/name for each device you have connected to your computer.  And furthermore, than name is consistent across reboots.  This is not only important for devs with multiple machines attached to a desktop, but critical in a lab situation.\n\nI realize that these changes were abandoned, but I wanted to put this here for future record.  Thanks.",
